  "oneLinerQuestion": "Design a Least Recently Used (LRU) cache supporting get and put in O(1) time.",
  "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/lru-cache/",
  "explanation": "Combine a Hash Map with a Doubly Linked List. The Hash Map provides O(1) node access by key. The Doubly Linked List maintains access history in O(1) time by removing and re-inserting accessed nodes at the MRU end (before the right sentinel) and evicting from the LRU end (after the left sentinel).",
  "pseudoCode": "CLASS LRUCache:\n    CONSTRUCTOR(capacity):\n        cap = capacity, cache = HASH_MAP(), left = Node(0,0), right = Node(0,0)\n        left.next = right; right.prev = left\n    FUNCTION get(key):\n        IF key IN cache THEN REMOVE(cache[key]); INSERT(cache[key]); RETURN cache[key].val\n        RETURN -1\n    FUNCTION put(key, value):\n        IF key IN cache THEN REMOVE(cache[key])\n        cache[key] = NEW Node(key, value); INSERT(cache[key])\n        IF LENGTH(cache) > cap THEN:\n            lru = left.next; REMOVE(lru); DELETE cache[lru.key]\nEND CLASS",
